## 6. Text mini mind-map (monetization model)

You can use this as a design checklist:

* **Monetization Core**

  * Subscriptions

    * Monthly VIP

      * Extra rewards (gems, chests)
      * Better Advance terms
      * Extra contract slots
      * VIP cosmetics / badge
    * Season Pass

      * Premium track
      * Exclusive cosmetics
      * Boosters & resources
  * Direct Purchases

    * Gem packs
    * Cosmetic bundles
    * Limited-time offers
  * Advance Challenges

    * Performance contracts (rank/wins)
    * Engagement contracts (days/quests)
    * Hybrid contracts
    * Settlement options (gems / partial loss / redemption quests)

* **Player Segments**

  * F2P grinders → Advance + occasional gem buy
  * Light spenders → Pass + occasional gem top-up
  * Whales → VIP + Pass + multiple Advances
  * Subscription lovers → VIP + optional challenges

* **Economy Tuning**

  * Base F2P progression works without spending
  * Advances = early access + challenge
  * Gem settlement priced below “full value”
  * Subs give comfort + small edge, not absolute dominance

